{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_142","type":"agent_message","text":"The BLAKE fixed-seed keypair matches C, isolating the mismatch to incremental hashing. The C source passes byte counts to a BLAKE update API that expects bit counts, so its transcript and message hashes intentionally process fractional/short bit lengths. A normal digest API cannot reproduce that bug; I’m replacing the wrapper with a direct pure-Rust BLAKE state/compression translation that preserves the erroneous bit-count calls exactly."}}
